## 4. Practical Lab Verification (Kali Linux)

### A. Symmetric AES-256-CBC Encryption with PBKDF2 Key Stretching (`openssl`)
Encrypting and decrypting a test payload using AES-256 in CBC mode with a random salt and PBKDF2 key derivation:

```text
$mkdir -p /tmp/secplus_crypto$ echo "TopSecret_SY0_701_Payload" > /tmp/secplus_crypto/secret.txt

# Encrypt using AES-256-CBC with salt and PBKDF2
$ openssl enc -aes-256-cbc -pbkdf2 -salt -in /tmp/secplus_crypto/secret.txt -out /tmp/secplus_crypto/secret.enc -pass pass:LabPass2026!

# Inspect encrypted binary header (starts with "Salted__")
$ head -c 16 /tmp/secplus_crypto/secret.enc | xxd
00000000: 5361 6c74 6564 5f5f 8a4f 12c9 7b3e 01d4  Salted__........

# Decrypt back to plaintext
$ openssl enc -d -aes-256-cbc -pbkdf2 -in /tmp/secplus_crypto/secret.enc -pass pass:LabPass2026!
TopSecret_SY0_701_Payload

$ rm -rf /tmp/secplus_crypto
