## 4. Practical Lab Verification (Kali Linux)

### Live TLS Certificate Chain & SAN Inspection (`openssl s_client`)
Inspecting a live TLS handshake to verify the certificate chain (Root → Intermediate → Leaf), public key algorithm, and Subject Alternative Names:

```text
# Connect via TLS and parse X.509 subject, issuer, validity, and SANs
$ openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com </dev/null 2>/dev/null \
  | openssl x509 -noout -subject -issuer -dates -ext subjectAltName

subject=CN = www.example.org
issuer=C = US, O = DigiCert Inc, CN = DigiCert Global G2 TLS RSA SHA256 2020 CA1
notBefore=Jan 15 00:00:00 2026 GMT
notAfter=Jan 15 23:59:59 2027 GMT
X509v3 Subject Alternative Name:
    DNS:www.example.org, DNS:example.com, DNS:example.net